# Where the outside pieces of the emulator and hardware test rigs live on this machine
# (tests/amiga, tests/warpos, tests/aros, tests/morphos; their README.md say what each is).
# Copy this file to tests/rig.conf, which git ignores, and set what you have. One KEY=value per
# line, no quotes, no comments after a value; a leading ~/ is your home. Variables set in the
# environment win over the file. RIG_CONF=path (in the environment) reads another file instead,
# e.g. one per machine.

# --- Amiga in WinUAE (tests/amiga/README.md) ---
# The emulator's tree: WinUAE builds (obj-winuae/, obj-winuae-sdl3/, obj-winuae-ppc/), the
# Kickstart ROM (rom/kick40068.A1200), AHI (aos/ahi/), the run work dirs (aos/work/xenon/).
#EMU=~/amiga-emu
# A Workbench 3.1 tree with Picasso96 installed (read only; runs copy what they need).
#WBDISK=/path/to/AmigaDisk
# Other WinUAE binary, Kickstart image:
#WINUAE=~/amiga-emu/obj-winuae-sdl3/winuae
#KICKSTART=~/amiga-emu/rom/kick40068.A1200

# --- WarpOS in WinUAE's Blizzard PPC (tests/warpos/README.md) ---
#WARPUP=~/amiga-sdk/WarpUP-5.1
#BPPC_ROM=~/amiga-emu/rom/blizzardppc_060_44.71.rom

# --- AROS (tests/aros/README.md) ---
# hosted/, native/ and contrib/ hold the unpacked 2026.09 releases, run/ the run dirs.
#AROS_DIR=/path/to/aros
# Single paths, if they are elsewhere (the defaults below AROS_DIR):
#AROS_HOSTED=/path/to/aros/hosted/AROS-202609-linux-x86_64-system
#AROS_ISO=/path/to/aros/native/AROS-202609-pc-x86_64-boot-iso/aros-pc-x86_64.iso
#AROS_RUNS=/path/to/aros/run
#CONTRIB=/path/to/aros/contrib/AROS-202609-any-x86_64-contrib

# --- MorphOS in QEMU pegasos2 (tests/morphos/README.md) ---
#MOS_DIR=/path/to/morphos

# --- A real A1200 on the network (tests/amiga/README.md "The real A1200") ---
# Its address (telnetd on port 2323), a directory this machine's web server serves, and the
# URL under which the A1200 sees that directory.
#A1200=a1200.lan
#A1200_WWW=/var/www/html/xenon
#A1200_URL=http://this-host.lan/xenon
